- TEST 01_DETECT_SIMPLE -
03.11.2010 / Niels Bassler <bassler@phys.au.dk> 
05.01.2012 / Armin Luehr <luehr@phys.au.dk>, updating input files and results

- DESCRIPTION:
This example is a test of SHIELD-HIT's new detector capabilities. The setup is a 400 MeV/u carbon ion beam hitting a 40 cm long water cylinder, radius 10 cm. The beam starts 2 cm before the cylinder. The scoring is realized in a cylinder of the same length but with a radius of 0.5 cm. The following hand calculated results refer to the entry position of the phantom, where the beam is still monoenergetic. LET is here both mass stopping power ( 1/rho * dE/dx ) and stopping power (dE/dx) since the density of water is set to 1 g/cm3.

The postprocessing script shield_detect2ascii will convert all results to ASCII files, which can be read by e.g. xmgrace.

Statistics: 10000.
Postprocessing results are in per primary particle.

CYL: radius = 0.5 cm, all phi, z = 40 cm, in 400 bins = 1 bin per mm.
MSH: 1 cm x 1 cm x 40 cm in 400 bins = 1 bin per mm.

- RESULTS:
*** DOSE AVERAGE LET ***
400 MeV/u carbon : 108.86 MeV cm2/g  = 10.886 keV/µm  (ICRU73: 108.9 keV/µm)
400 MeV   protons: 3.032  MeV cm2/g  = 0.3032 keV/µm  (pstar: 0.3031 keV/µm)

*** TRACK AVERAGE LET ***
Same as above since the beam is monoenergetic.


*** FLUENCE PER PARTICLE ***
  1 / (r*r*PI) = 1.2732 cm-2

*** LET WEIGHTED FLUENCE ***
 same as fluence.

*** CROSSING NUMBER OF PARTICLES PER PRIMARY ***
 One (one particle crossing the surface).

*** ENERGY PER PARTICLE ***
 bin width * LET * rho = 0.1 cm * 108.86 MeV cm2 /g * 1 g/cm3 = 10.886 MeV

*** DOSE ***
 LET * fluence = 108.86 MeV cm2 /g * 1.2732 cm-2 = 138.6 MeV/g
 138.6 MeV/g * 1.60217646e-10 (g/MeV)(J/kg) = 2.220625e-8 Gy

*** AVERAGE ENERGY ***
 400 MeV/u

*** LETFLU ***
Equals dose since medium is set to target.

- REMARKS: